# Laboratorium 1: testy HTTP w JetBrains Rider (HTTP Client)
# Zmien port, jeśli Rider uruchamia aplikacje pod innym adresem.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5109

### Hello
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/Hello

### Status 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/Status?code=404

### Status 418
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/Status?code=418

### Status 500
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/Status?code=500

### Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/Details/3

### Echo
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/Echo?name=Ala&count=2

### Square
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/Square/7

### Inspect
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/Inspect

### Sum (poprawne)
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/Sum?a=2&b=3

### Sum (bledne a, oczekiwane 400 z kontrola ModelState)
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/Sum?a=x&b=3

### UserAgent
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/UserAgent

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/Health

### Import - JSON, oczekiwane 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/Book/Import
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Solaris", "isbn": "9788308065341", "price": 39.9 }

### Import - text/plain, oczekiwane 415
POST {{baseUrl}}/Book/Import
Content-Type: text/plain

{ "title": "Solaris", "isbn": "9788308065341", "price": 39.9 }

### Import - GET, oczekiwane 405
GET {{baseUrl}}/Book/Import
